      "concept": {
        "summary": "Reminder: extra electrons form lone pairs. Not enough electrons means extra bonds (double or triple).",
        "keyIdeas": [
          "Count bonding pairs and lone pairs on the CENTRAL atom only. A double or triple bond counts as ONE bonding pair when you name the shape.",
          "Domains = bonding pairs + lone pairs. Use your VSEPR reference to name the shape and give the bond angle."
