      "keyNotes": [
        "Bonding pairs = bonds to the central atom, a double or triple bond counted once (domains). Lone pairs = on the central atom only.",
        "Octet exception: PCl₅. P holds 10 electrons (5 bonds), so P exceeds the octet; period 3 atoms can.",
        "Double and triple bonds: CO₂ (two C=O), CH₂O (C=O), HCN (C≡N), SO₂ (one S=O, the octet-rule structure).",
        "Repeated shapes on purpose: linear (CO₂ vs HCN), trigonal pyramidal (NH₃ vs PCl₃), bent (H₂O and OF₂ from 4 domains; SO₂ from 3 domains).",
        "Angles with lone pairs are given as “less than”; accept the familiar values (NH₃ 107°, H₂O 104.5°)."
      ]
    }
